From: MUHAMMAD ALIF DANIEL BIN MOHD HAIRUL HEZZELIN
 <alifdaniel.personalspace@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] recovery: Format data on an Android factory reset

Erase all data in Android settings reboots to recovery with --wipe_data.
TWRP turned that into "wipe data", which keeps /data/media. Its files are
still encrypted with the old user keys, so vold fails to set up the new
user and the ROM loops back to recovery. Format data instead, as the stock
recovery does.
---
 startup/startup_args.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/startup/startup_args.cpp b/startup/startup_args.cpp
index 34cb650..ad6e321 100755
--- a/startup/startup_args.cpp
+++ b/startup/startup_args.cpp
@@ -87,7 +87,11 @@ bool StartupArgs::ProcessRecoveryArgs(const std::vector<std::string>& args, cons
       send_intent_ = value;
     }
   } else if (arg.starts_with(kWipeData)) {
-    if (!OpenRecoveryScript::Insert_ORS_Command("wipe data\n")) return false;
+    // A factory reset from Android must leave no user data behind, as the
+    // stock recovery does. Wiping data keeps /data/media, whose files are
+    // still encrypted with the old user keys, and vold then fails to set up
+    // the new user and the ROM loops back to recovery.
+    if (!OpenRecoveryScript::Insert_ORS_Command("format data\n")) return false;
   } else if (arg.starts_with(kWipeCache)) {
     if (!OpenRecoveryScript::Insert_ORS_Command("wipe cache\n")) return false;
   } else if (arg.starts_with(kNandroid)) {
